  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 718f67b7b841dde4a89478ad5ef11627, type: 3}
  m_Name: Dialogue_Ch2_6_Knife
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Zmywak.Narrative::Zmywak.Narrative.Dialogue.DialogueGraph
  startNodeId: knife_1
  nodes:
  - nodeId: knife_1
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "\u015Aroda, przed otwarciem. Declan staje przy zlewie z no\u017Cem szefa kuchni w r\u0119ce i workiem cebuli pod pach\u0105."
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: Our prep cook is gone back to Cork. Can you hold a knife, Kooba?
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Czy umiem trzyma\u0107 n\xF3\u017C. Pi\u0119\u0107 lat filozofii i nikt mnie o to nie zapyta\u0142."
    teachVocabularyWords:
    - prep
    - cook
    - gone
    - hold
    - knife
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: ch2_covered_tunde
    branchNodeId: knife_tunde
    nextNodeId: knife_try
  - nodeId: knife_tunde
    lines:
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: And about Sunday. Tunde told me. You're sound, Kooba. That's why I'm asking you.
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "\"Sound\". Po minie Declana poznaj\u0119, \u017Ce to komplement. Chyba najwi\u0119kszy, jaki ma na stanie."
    teachVocabularyWords:
    - told
    - asking
    unlockSlangIds:
    - slang_sound
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 5
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: knife_try
  - nodeId: knife_try
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Deska, cebula, n\xF3\u017C. Declan pokazuje raz: palce zgi\u0119te jak pazury, ostrze prowadzi k\u0142ykie\u0107. Dziesi\u0119\u0107 cebul p\xF3\u017Aniej Kuba p\u0142acze, ale nie ze smutku."
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: Not bad. Not good either. Two hours of prep before every shift, the sink after. Same money for now. Deal?
    teachVocabularyWords:
    - bad
    - either
    - hours
    - every
    - money
    - deal
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices:
    - choiceText: "Bior\u0119. Od zlewu do deski - to jest kariera."
      targetNodeId: knife_yes
      requiredFlag: 
    - choiceText: "Prosz\u0119 o tydzie\u0144 do namys\u0142u."
      targetNodeId: knife_wait
      requiredFlag: 
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
  - nodeId: knife_yes
    lines:
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: Good man. Tomorrow, nine. Bring your own plasters.
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Syzyf dosta\u0142 nowy kamie\u0144. Mniejszy, ostrzejszy i pachn\u0105cy cebul\u0105. Wyobra\u017Cam go sobie szcz\u0119\u015Bliwym. Tym razem dzia\u0142a."
    teachVocabularyWords:
    - plasters
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch2_prep_cook
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: -5
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 5
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: knife_end
  - nodeId: knife_wait
    lines:
    - speakerId: declan
      language: 1
      text: A week? Fair enough. The onions will wait. I won't, so don't be long.
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Nie wiem, dlaczego si\u0119 waham. Mo\u017Ce dlatego, \u017Ce przy zlewie wiem, kim jestem. A za desk\u0105 nie wiem jeszcze nic."
    teachVocabularyWords:
    - fair
    - enough
    - wait
    - long
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags:
    - ch2_prep_later
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: 0
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: knife_end
  - nodeId: knife_end
    lines:
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Wieczorem budka telefoniczna na rogu Phibsborough Road. Karta za pi\u0119\u0107 euro, dwana\u015Bcie minut do Polski."
    - speakerId: mum
      language: 0
      text: "Kubu\u015B, chc\u0105 ci\u0119 na kucharza? M\xF3j syn, kucharz w Dublinie! Ojciec m\xF3wi, \u017Ce w rodzinie zawsze by\u0142 talent do no\u017Ca. Po dziadku rze\u017Aniku."
    - speakerId: kuba_thought
      language: 0
      text: "Drugi tydzie\u0144 w Dublinie: pierwsza koperta, pierwsze irlandzkie s\u0142owa, pierwsza cebula. Brudne talerze dalej czekaj\u0105. Ale kto\u015B zobaczy\u0142, \u017Ce umiem co\u015B wi\u0119cej."
    - speakerId: narrator
      language: 0
      text: "Koniec Rozdzia\u0142u 2: Pierwsza wyp\u0142ata."
    teachVocabularyWords: []
    unlockSlangIds: []
    setFlags: []
    outcome:
      moneyEuros: 0
      energy: 0
      homesickness: -10
      integration: 0
    choices: []
    branchIfFlag: 
    branchNodeId: 
    nextNodeId: 
